{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--causative-allomorphy-conditioning","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--allomorphy"],"statement":{"en":"The productive causative suffix is phonologically conditioned as -re after vowels and /y/, -e after /r/, and -te after other consonants.","ja":"生産的使役接尾辞は音韻論的に条件づけられ、母音および /y/ の後で -re、/r/ の後で -e、その他の子音の後で -te となる。"},"type":"alternation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":["-re","-e","-te"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0005-04","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2022@handbook-epub/l0134-18","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0033-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--causative-allomorphy-conditioning-shizunai","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--allomorphy"],"statement":{"en":"In Shizunai, verbs ending in -y or a vowel take the causative allomorph -re, verbs ending in -r take -e, and verbs ending in other consonants take -te.","ja":"静内方言において、-y または母音で終わる動詞は使役異形態 -re を、-r で終わる動詞は -e を、その他の子音で終わる動詞は -te をとる。"},"type":"alternation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":["-re","-e","-te"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0182-04","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0182-05","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0182-06","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0183-03","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0183-04","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0183-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--causative-allomorphy-conditioning","differs_in":"dialect","note":"Restricted to Shizunai dialect"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--causative-allomorphy-conditioning-consonant-types","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--allomorphy"],"statement":{"en":"The causative allomorph -re attaches after vowels, y, and w; -te attaches after other consonants (p, t, k, s, m, n); and -e attaches after r.","ja":"使役接尾辞は、母音および y, w の後では -re、その他の子音（p, t, k, s, m, n）の後では -te、r の後では -e が付加される。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":["-re","-te","-e"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0197-02","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0252-02","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0253-01","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0254-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--causative-allomorphy-conditioning","differs_in":null,"note":"Explicitly details stem-final w grouping with vowels/y and lists consonant phonemes p, t, k, s, m, n"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--traditional-conditioning-causative-allomorphs","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--allomorphy"],"statement":{"en":"The causative suffix surfaces as -re after vowel-final stems, -e after r-final stems, and -te after stems ending in consonants other than r.","ja":"語幹が母音で終わる動詞には -re、r で終わる動詞には -e、r 以外の子音で終わる動詞には -te が付く。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":["-re","-e","-te"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0135-03","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0136-01","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0136-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--causative-allomorphy-conditioning","differs_in":"framework","note":"Traditional orthographic-level description omitting semivowel conditioning"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--causative-valency-increase-plus-one","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--arity"],"statement":{"en":"The morphological causative suffixes (-re / -e / -te) increase the verb's arity by one, turning the base subject into an object while introducing the causer as the new subject.","ja":"使役接尾辞（-re / -e / -te）は動詞の項結合価を1増やし、元の主語を目的語とし、使役者を新たな主語として導入する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":["-re","-e","-te"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0008-06","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0197-01","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0427-01","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0033-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--three-place-verb-causativization-four-place","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--arity"],"statement":{"en":"When a three-place verb is causativized by a causative suffix, a four-place verb construction results.","ja":"3項動詞が使役接尾辞によって使役化されると、4項動詞構文が形成される。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":["-re"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0136-03","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0137-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--verbal-number-agreement-causee","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--arity"],"statement":{"en":"In causative verbs derived from intransitive verbs with a number distinction, verbal number plurality agrees with the original intransitive agent (the causee object) rather than with the grammatical subject.","ja":"数区別を持つ自動詞から派生した使役動詞において、動詞の数の複数性は文法上の主語ではなく元の動詞の動作主（被使役者目的語）と一致する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"asserted","conditions":["stem has number distinction"]},"forms":["-re","-te"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2022@handbook-epub/l0112-09","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2022@handbook-epub/l0113-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--productive-causative-both-direct-and-indirect","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--direct-indirect"],"statement":{"en":"The productive causative suffix -re/-e/-te derives both direct and indirect causatives.","ja":"生産的な使役接尾辞 -re/-e/-te は直接使役と間接使役の双方を派生する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":["-re","-e","-te"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0005-05","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0010-05","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0013-04","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:bugaevakobayashi2022@handbook-epub/l0102-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--causative-permissive-and-coercive","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--direct-indirect"],"statement":{"en":"Morphological causatives in Ainu can express both coercive causation and permissive causation.","ja":"アイヌ語の形態論的使役は、強制使役と許容使役（許可）の双方を表すことができる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":["-re","-e","-te"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0008-03","stance":"reports"},{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0008-04","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0254-02","stance":"proposes"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--causee-rejects-incorporation-and-antipassivization","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--direct-indirect"],"statement":{"en":"In indirect causatives, the causee object never undergoes noun incorporation or antipassivization.","ja":"間接使役において、被使役者目的語は決して名詞抱合や逆受動化を受けない。"},"type":"absence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0009-02","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0009-04","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0011-07","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--motion-verbs-causative-ke-singular-te-plural","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--motion-verbs"],"statement":{"en":"Motion verbs take -ke as their causative suffix in the singular, matching plural causatives in -te.","ja":"移動動詞では単数形の使役接尾辞として -ke が用いられ、複数形の使役接尾辞 -te と対応する。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":["-ke","-te"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0146-01","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0198-03","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0253-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--traditional-recognition-productive-and-indefinite-only","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--overview"],"statement":{"en":"In traditional analyses of Ainu grammar, only the productive suffix -re/-e/-te and the indefinite causative -yar/-ar are recognized as causative markers.","ja":"アイヌ語の伝統文法分析では、生産的な接尾辞 -re/-e/-te と不定使役の -yar/-ar のみが使役標識として認められてきた。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"reported","conditions":[]},"forms":["-re","-e","-te","-yar","-ar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2012@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0014-07","stance":"reports"},{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0001-03","stance":"reports"},{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0013-01","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--productive-vs-unproductive-causative-classification","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--productivity"],"statement":{"en":"Valency-increasing causatives in Ainu are divided into productive causatives (-re/-e/-te) and non-productive causatives (-V, -ke, -ka).","ja":"アイヌ語の結合価増大使役は、生産的な使役（-re/-e/-te）と非生産的な使役（-V, -ke, -ka）に分類される。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":["-re","-e","-te","-V","-ke","-ka"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0010-04","stance":"proposes"},{"id":"stmt:bugaevakobayashi2022@handbook-epub/l0100-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--weather-verbs-reject-productive-causative","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--productivity"],"statement":{"en":"Avalent meteorological verbs that have incorporated their subjects reject productive causativization with -re/-e/-te.","ja":"主語を抱合した無項の気象動詞は、-re/-e/-te による生産的な使役化を許容しない。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":["-re","-e","-te"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaevakobayashi2022@handbook-epub/l0100-07","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0005-06","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0011-08","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--replacement-of-ka-by-productive-causative","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--diachrony"],"statement":{"en":"The non-productive causative function of -ka is gradually being replaced cross-dialectally by the productive causative suffix -re/-e/-te as the default causative marker.","ja":"-ka による非生産的な使役機能は、デフォルトの使役標識である生産的な使役接尾辞 -re/-e/-te によって方言横断的に徐々に置き換えられつつある。"},"type":"diachrony","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"proposes","conditions":[]},"forms":["-ka","-re","-e","-te"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0010-07","stance":"proposes"},{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0013-05","stance":"proposes"},{"id":"stmt:bugaevakobayashi2022@handbook-epub/l0100-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--ke-derives-from-one-arg-only","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--productivity"],"statement":{"en":"Non-productive causatives in -ke derive only from one-argument verbs, whereas -V, -ka, and -re/-e/-te can derive causatives from both one-argument and two-argument verbs.","ja":"非生産的な -ke 使役は1項動詞からのみ派生するのに対し、-V, -ka, -re/-e/-te は1項動詞および2項動詞の双方から使役を派生できる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":["-ke","-V","-ka","-re","-e","-te"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0011-02","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:bugaevakobayashi2022@handbook-epub/l0100-08","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--when-a-causative-verb-is-used-in-an","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te"],"statement":{"en":"When a causative verb is used in an imperative addressed to multiple people, the sentence-final particle yan can cooccur with a singular verb stem whose semantic causee is singular.","ja":"使役動詞が複数人に対する命令で用いられる場合、意味上の被使役者が単数であれば、終助詞 yan は動詞の単数形語幹と共起できる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":["causative verbs in plural imperative clauses"]},"forms":["-te","yan"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2022@handbook-epub/l0112-12","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--causative-forms-combining-two-personal-prefixes-such-as","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te"],"statement":{"en":"Causative forms combining two personal prefixes such as *en-e-raykere (intended 'he makes me kill you') are unacceptable and unattested in Ainu.","ja":"＊en-e-raykere（彼が私にお前を殺させる）のように人称接頭辞が2つ重なる使役形式は容認されず、文献資料にも見られない。"},"type":"judgement","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"none","modality":"necessary","conditions":[]},"forms":["*en-e-raykere"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2023b@pdftotext-pieces/l0003-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--the-stative-verb-kiyanne-be-older-forms-the","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--allomorphy"],"statement":{"en":"The stative verb kiyanne 'be older' forms the causative kiyanne-re 'treat someone as an elder / host someone respectfully'.","ja":"状態動詞 kiyanne「年上である」は使役形 kiyanne-re を作って「〜を大切にもてなす（相手を年長者として遇する）」という表現を作ることができる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["kiyanne","kiyanne-re","-re"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0117-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--in-ainu-causative-verbs-meaning-make-someone-do","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--allomorphy"],"statement":{"en":"In Ainu, causative verbs meaning 'make someone do ...' are formed by attaching suffixes such as -re, -te, -ka, or -e to verbs, with suffix selection largely determined by the stem-final sound.","ja":"アイヌ語では、動詞に -re, -te, -ka, -e のような接尾辞を付けて使役の意味を表す動詞を作り、どの接尾辞が付くかは語幹末尾の音によって大体決まっている。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-re","-te","-ka","-e"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0252-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--the-causative-suffix-re-te-attaches-before-vowel","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--allomorphy"],"statement":{"en":"The causative suffix -re/-te attaches before vowel addition to final r, appearing as -te after nukar and kor and triggering the change of syllable-final r to n.","ja":"使役接尾辞-re/-teは語末rへの母音添加の前に付加され、nukarやkorの後では-teとなり、音節末rはnに変化する。"},"type":"ordering","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-re","-te","nukan-te","kon-te"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:tangiku2022@handbook-epub/l0055-13","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--the-ainu-verb-ikure-to-make-someone-drink","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--allomorphy"],"statement":{"en":"The Ainu verb ikure 'to make someone drink sake' is morphologically derived from the object prefix i-, the verb ku 'drink', and the causative suffix -re.","ja":"アイヌ語の動詞 ikure「（人に）酒を飲ませる」は、目的語接頭辞 i-、動詞 ku「飲む」、使役接尾辞 -re から形態論的に派生している。"},"type":"diachrony","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["ikure","i-","ku","-re"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:vovin2022@handbook-epub/l0040-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--in-direct-causativization-of-transitive-verbs-with-re","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--arity"],"statement":{"en":"In direct causativization of transitive verbs with -re/-e/-te, the original object is retained and the original subject (the causee argument) also becomes an object, resulting in a double-object construction.","ja":"他動詞の-re/-e/-teによる使役化の場合、元の目的語（O）が保たれ、かつ元の主語（被使役者となる項）も目的語（Oc）となって二重目的語構造が作られる。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":["direct causativization of transitive verbs with -re/-e/-te"]},"forms":["-re","-e","-te"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0007-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--in-causative-clauses-based-on-transitive-verbs-omission","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--arity"],"statement":{"en":"In causative clauses based on transitive verbs, omission of the causee object occurs frequently when it is clear from context, but if the original base object is obvious, it is omitted instead.","ja":"他動詞に基づく使役構文では、被使役者目的語が文脈上明らかな場合にその省略がしばしば起こる一方、元の目的語の方が明白であればそちらが省略される。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":["causatives of transitive verbs"]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0007-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--transitive-verbs-undergoing-indirect-causativization-become-trivalent-verbs","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--arity"],"statement":{"en":"Transitive verbs undergoing indirect causativization become trivalent verbs with a double-object structure.","ja":"間接使役化された他動詞は統語的に三項動詞になり、二重目的語構造をとる。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-re","-e","-te"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0009-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--in-ainu-direct-causative-verbs-formed-with-unproductive","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--arity"],"statement":{"en":"In Ainu, direct causative verbs formed with unproductive -V, -ke or productive -re/-e/-te can further take -re/-e/-te to express indirect causation, yielding double causative verbs.","ja":"アイヌ語では非生産的な-V, -keや生産的な-re/-e/-teによる直接使役動詞に、さらに-re/-e/-teが付いて間接使役を表すことが可能であり、二重使役動詞を形成する。"},"type":"existence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"possible","conditions":[]},"forms":["-re","-e","-te","-V","-ke"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0009-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--double-causatives-in-ainu-are-expressed-in-a","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--arity"],"statement":{"en":"Double causatives in Ainu are expressed in a double-object construction with two unmarked objects.","ja":"アイヌ語の二重使役は、無標の目的語を2つ伴った二重目的語構造で表される。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0010-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--in-ainu-double-causativization-of-transitive-verbs-is","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--arity"],"statement":{"en":"In Ainu, double causativization of transitive verbs is possible, yielding four-place verbs, although such verbs are extremely rare.","ja":"アイヌ語では他動詞の二重使役化すら可能であり、その結果四項動詞ができるが、これは非常に稀である。"},"type":"existence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-re","-e","-te"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0010-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--causative-derivatives-of-2-argument-locative-object-verbs","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--arity"],"statement":{"en":"Causative derivatives of 2-argument locative object verbs, such as omare, osmare, and kuste, are commonly used as 3-argument locative object verbs.","ja":"2項動詞に使役接尾辞がついた omare, osmare, kuste などの3項動詞も場所目的語動詞としてよく使われる。"},"type":"membership","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["omare","osmare","kuste"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0209-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--causative-suffix-re-has-an-arity-of-1","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--arity"],"statement":{"en":"Causative suffix -re has an arity of +1, whereas causative suffix -yar has an arity of 0.","ja":"使役接尾辞 -re のアリティは +1 であり、使役接尾辞 -yar のアリティは 0 である。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-re","-yar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0363-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--when-a-causative-suffix-is-added-to-an","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--arity"],"statement":{"en":"When a causative suffix is added to an intransitive verb whose subject is first person, the original subject marker ku= changes to the object marker en=.","ja":"1人称が主語の自動詞に使役接尾辞が付くと、元の主語接辞 ku= は目的語接辞 en= に交替する。"},"type":"alternation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"necessary","conditions":["1人称主語の自動詞使役化において"]},"forms":["ku=","en="],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0427-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--the-causative-verbs-kore-sg-and-korpare-pl","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--arity"],"statement":{"en":"The causative verbs kore (sg) and korpare (pl) express the number of the indirect object (causee), reflecting the number of the subject of kor / korpa before causativization.","ja":"使役動詞 kore（単数）と korpare（複数）は間接目的語の単複を表すが，これは使役化前の主語の単複が被使役者の単複として現れたものである。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/chitose"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["kore","korpare"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0121-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--the-verb-omare-put-into-is-a-causative","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--arity"],"statement":{"en":"The verb omare 'put into' is a causative formation ('make enter') in which the theme is the direct object (causee).","ja":"動詞 omare「～に入れる」は「～に入らせる」という使役形であり、主題が直接目的語（被使役者）である。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["omare"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2023b@pdftotext-pieces/l0002-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--in-southwestern-hokkaido-dialects-a-few-intransitive-verbs","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--diachrony"],"statement":{"en":"In Southwestern Hokkaido dialects, a few intransitive verbs are recorded with both -re/-e/-te and -ka causative derivations without semantic difference.","ja":"北海道南西部方言でも幾つかの自動詞は、意味的に差のない-re/-e/-teと-kaの両方の派生形が記録されている。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest"],"quantifier":"exists","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-re","-e","-te","-ka"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0005-09","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--sakhalin-ainu-attests-the-reflexive-causative-form-yay","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--diachrony"],"statement":{"en":"Sakhalin Ainu attests the reflexive-causative form yay-monax-te meaning 'to keep oneself awake'.","ja":"樺太アイヌ語には「目を覚ましておく」を意味する再帰使役形 yay-monax-te が証言されている。"},"type":"existence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["yay-monax-te"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:vovin2022@handbook-epub/l0039-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--intransitive-verbs-from-which-direct-causatives-are-derived","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--direct-indirect"],"statement":{"en":"Intransitive verbs from which direct causatives are derived by -re/-e/-te fall into two groups: non-derived intransitive verbs expressing properties or internal states/processes, and derived intransitive verbs (including those diachronically derived).","ja":"-re/-e/-teによって直接使役が派生される自動詞には、性質や内的状態／過程を表す非派生自動詞と、（通時的なものを含めた）派生自動詞の2つのグループがある。"},"type":"membership","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":["derived with -re/-e/-te"]},"forms":["-re","-e","-te"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0006-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--derived-intransitive-verbs-that-take-re-e-te","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--direct-indirect"],"statement":{"en":"Derived intransitive verbs that take -re/-e/-te to form direct causatives comprise antipassive verbs with i-, lexicalized reflexive-possessive verbs, and autocausative (body-movement) verbs derived with the prefixes he- 'head' and ho- 'buttocks'.","ja":"-re/-e/-teにより直接使役が派生される派生自動詞には、接頭辞i-による逆受動動詞、語彙化した再帰所有動詞、および接頭辞he-「頭、上部」やho-「尻、末端」により派生された自己使役（身体動作）動詞が含まれる。"},"type":"membership","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":["derived intransitive verbs taking -re/-e/-te"]},"forms":["i-","he-","ho-","-re","-e","-te"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0006-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--all-base-transitive-verbs-that-undergo-direct-causativization","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--direct-indirect"],"statement":{"en":"All base transitive verbs that undergo direct causativization with -re/-e/-te have non-agentive subjects.","ja":"-re/-e/-teによって直接使役化される基底の他動詞は、すべて非動作主的な主語を持つ。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":["base transitive verbs taking -re/-e/-te direct causative"]},"forms":["-re","-e","-te"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0007-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--indirect-causatives-in-ainu-can-be-derived-from","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--direct-indirect"],"statement":{"en":"Indirect causatives in Ainu can be derived from transitive verbs as well as agentive intransitive verbs using the suffix -re/-e/-te.","ja":"-re/-e/-teによる間接使役は、他動詞からも動作的自動詞からも派生される。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-re","-e","-te"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0008-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--according-to-fukuda-tamura-2001-the-suffix-re","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--direct-indirect"],"statement":{"en":"According to Fukuda (Tamura) (2001), the suffix -re/-e/-te implies only coercive causation, where the causer makes the causee do something regardless of the causee's volition.","ja":"福田（田村）（2001）によれば、-re/-e/-teは被使役者の意志・意向とは関係なしに使役主が被使役者に何かをさせるという強制使役の意味のみを含意する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-re","-e","-te"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0008-02","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--all-intransitive-verb-stems-that-undergo-indirect-causativization","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--direct-indirect"],"statement":{"en":"All intransitive verb stems that undergo indirect causativization with -re/-e/-te take animate or agentive subjects.","ja":"-re/-e/-teにより間接使役化される自動詞語基は全て、有生の主語か動作主的な主語をとるものである。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-re","-e","-te"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0008-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--indirect-causatives-with-re-e-te-can-be","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--direct-indirect"],"statement":{"en":"Indirect causatives with -re/-e/-te can be derived from intransitive verbs formed by object incorporation.","ja":"-re/-e/-teによる間接使役は、他動詞が元の目的語を抱合した派生自動詞からも派生される。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"exists","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-re","-e","-te"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0008-07","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--depending-on-whether-the-undergoer-is-interpreted-as","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--direct-indirect"],"statement":{"en":"Depending on whether the undergoer is interpreted as agentive or not, certain verbs causativized with -re/-e/-te can be interpreted as either direct or indirect causatives.","ja":"被動作者を動作主的であると解釈するかそうでないかによって、-re/-e/-teによる直接使役とも間接使役とも解釈されうる動詞がある。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"exists","modality":"possible","conditions":[]},"forms":["-re","-e","-te"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0008-08","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--when-the-productive-causative-re-e-te-attaches","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--direct-indirect"],"statement":{"en":"When the productive causative -re/-e/-te attaches to ingestion verbs, both direct causative and indirect causative interpretations are permitted depending on the semantic properties of the causee.","ja":"摂取動詞に-re/-e/-teが付いた場合は、被使役者ごとの意味特性に合わせて直接使役と間接使役の両解釈が許される。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":["with ingestion verbs"]},"forms":["-re","-e","-te"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0010-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--in-direct-causatives-with-ka-and-re-e","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--direct-indirect"],"statement":{"en":"In direct causatives with -ka and -re/-e/-te, non-referential direct causees can be backgrounded through noun incorporation or antipassivization.","ja":"-ka及び-re/-e/-teによる直接使役の場合、指示的でない直接被使役者は抱合あるいは逆受動化によって背景化される。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"possible","conditions":["with non-referential direct causees in direct causatives with -ka or -re/-e/-te"]},"forms":["-ka","-re","-e","-te"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0011-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--for-the-one-argument-verb-as-stand-two","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--direct-indirect"],"statement":{"en":"For the one-argument verb as 'stand', two causative forms exist: direct causative as-i (with suffix -i) corresponding to a Theme subject, and indirect causative as-te (with productive suffix -te) corresponding to an Agent subject.","ja":"1項動詞 as「立つ」には2種類の使役形が存在し、対象（Theme）主語に対応する直接使役形 as-i（接尾辞 -i）と、動作主主語に対応する間接使役形 as-te（生産的接尾辞 -te）がある。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"example_only","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["as","as-i","as-te","-i","-te"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaevakobayashi2022@handbook-epub/l0101-12","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--when-the-causee-of-an-n-final-intransitive","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--motion-verbs"],"statement":{"en":"When the causee of an n-final intransitive motion verb is agentive, the verb can be transitivized into an indirect causative with -re/-e/-te.","ja":"同様のnで終わる移動動詞は被使役者が動作主的である場合には、-re/-e/-teで間接使役化されうる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"possible","conditions":["causee is agentive"]},"forms":["-re","-e","-te"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0004-09","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--as-a-direct-causative-marker-re-e-te","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--overview"],"statement":{"en":"As a direct causative marker, -re/-e/-te is basically in complementary distribution with the causative suffixes -V, -ka, and -ke, and cannot attach to verbs or roots that take them.","ja":"直接使役の標識としての-re/-e/-teは、使役接尾辞-V, -ka, -keの付く動詞や語根には基本的に付加できず、これら4つの標識は相補分布している。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"usually","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-re","-e","-te","-V","-ka","-ke"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0005-07","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--causative-verbs-can-be-formed-from-intransitive-and","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--overview"],"statement":{"en":"Causative verbs can be formed from intransitive and transitive verb stems by suffixing -re (-te, -e) or sometimes -ka.","ja":"使役形は、接尾辞-re（-te, -e）、あるいは時に-kaを付加することによって、自動詞語幹および他動詞語幹の双方から派生できる。"},"type":"existence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-re","-te","-e","-ka"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2022@handbook-epub/l0113-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--chiri-analyzes-the-causative-suffixes-re-and-te","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--overview"],"statement":{"en":"Chiri analyzes the causative suffixes -re and -te as transitivizing in some cases and causativizing in others.","ja":"知里は使役接尾辞 -re および -te をある場合には他動詞化接尾辞、別の場合には使役接尾辞として解釈している。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-re","-te"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0026-05","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--adjunct-increasing-suffixes-either-turn-intransitive-verbs-into","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--overview"],"statement":{"en":"Adjunct-increasing suffixes either turn intransitive verbs into transitive verbs or express the causative.","ja":"副加語増加接尾辞は、自動詞を他動詞に変えるか、使役を表す。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0072-13","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--in-verbs-that-form-direct-causatives-with-the","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--productivity"],"statement":{"en":"In verbs that form direct causatives with the unproductive suffixes -V or -ke, the productive causative suffix -re/-e/-te is always interpreted as an indirect causative marker.","ja":"非生産的な接尾辞-V, -keによって直接使役を作る動詞では、生産的使役標識-re/-e/-teは必ず間接使役の標識として解釈される。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"necessary","conditions":["with verbs forming direct causatives via -V or -ke"]},"forms":["-re","-e","-te","-ke","-V"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0009-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--when-ke-and-re-te-e-both-form","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topics":["topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te","topic:valency/causative-morphological-re-e-te--productivity"],"statement":{"en":"When -ke and -re (-te, -e) both form causative pairs on the same verb stem, -ke is often used for inanimate objects, whereas -re is basically used for animate or volitional entities like humans.","ja":"-ke と -re (-te, -e) が同一の動詞について使役形を作る場合、-ke は物に対して使われることが多く、-re は基本的に人間など意志のあるものに対して使われる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"usually","modality":"actual","conditions":["when both suffixes attach to the same verb stem"]},"forms":["-ke","-re","-te","-e"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0199-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
